    "updated_at": "2026-11-28T00:27:42Z",
    "body": "Two more requirements for the pattern checks:\n\n1. **Stale results.** A change to a source operation in a pattern folder makes all copies of that operation stale. A stock simulation or a verification result of the old version must not count for the new version. The post refuses until the copies are generated and checked again.\n2. **Comparison scope.** The diagnostic states which model the gouge check uses (the part model of the setup). The check must never be skipped without a word. Example: the part model holds only the first copy, and the other copies cut where the model has no feature. The post either judges each copy against the full model, or it says that the copies outside the model are judged against the stock only.\n\nDone means adds: a test that edits the source operation and shows that the old simulation result no longer lets the post pass.\n",
